  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Livelihood status of the people at Arato and Maytsedo PA of Enderta Woreda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project site Arato and Maytsedo Peasant Associations (PAs) is located in Enderta Woreda/district, Tigray Region. This area is one of the drought prone and food insecure areas in the Region. According to the rapid needs assessment done by ADCS in the two Peasant Associations poor crop and livestock production and productivity; dependency on rain-fed cultivation and erratic pattern of rainfall; less income opportunity of the community other than crop production; Natural Resource Degradation and Poor Management of Existing Natural Resources and shortage of potable water were identified. Based on these facts, the main goal of the project is to contribute to the attainment of food security in a sustainable manner for the community of Arato and Maytsedo PAs of the woreda/district. 
The project will focus on building water reservoir and  irrigation canals, provision of training on different agricultural practice including agribusiness; rehabilitation of galleys by constructing check dams and enriching the existing closure areas and introduction of cut and carry livestock feeding system; diversify the income opportunity of targeted beneficiaries by providing Shoats, improved poultry breeds, Begait Cows(improved local diary cows ) and bee-colonies; and construction of  four boreholes and three hand dug wells.
The project is a three year project and it is expected that 2660 HH are going to benefit directly from the project.</narrative>
  </description>
